  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Nevada has recorded $276M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state logged 453 awards with an average award size of $610K. Obligations fell 92.5% year over year. The Department of Energy is the top buyer with $225M in obligations. MISSION SUPPORT & TEST SERVICES LLC is the top vendor with $225M in obligations. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligations at $226M. Historical annual obligations show larger totals in earlier years: FY22 was $3.3B, FY23 was $3.8B, FY24 was $4.1B, FY25 was $4.1B, and FY26 was $3.7B. FY2027 to date totals are partial (fiscal year to date). These figures show that most FY2027 to date spending is concentrated in a few large awards and buyers, while overall state obligations are much smaller than recent full-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal spending in Nevada this year?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy obligated $225M, which accounts for the majority of the $276M total. MISSION SUPPORT & TEST SERVICES LLC received $225M, reflecting concentration among vendors. Facilities Support Services received $226M, indicating a single industry dominates obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with recent full fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations are $276M compared with $3.3B in FY22, $3.8B in FY23, $4.1B in FY24, $4.1B in FY25, and $3.7B in FY26. Obligations fell 92.5% year over year. FY2027 to date totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
      }
    ]
  },
